<title>AUSTRALIA: PNG's Mt Kare gold deposit up to 100m deep - partner.</title>
<headline>PNG's Mt Kare gold deposit up to 100m deep - partner.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian mining group Madison Enterprises Corp released on Wednesday drilling results from the Mount Kare gold prospect in Papua New Guinea showing mineralisations up to 100 metres deep.</p>
<p>&quot;Based in the recent drilling it appears that northernly trending structures...the disposition of near surface gold and silver mineralisation that is blanket-like and generally flat-lying in form and up to 100 metres in thickness,&quot; Madison said in a statement released by Mount Kare partner Carpenter Pacific Resources NL.</p>
</text>
